        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void syn_x25519</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint8_t shared_out[32], const uint8_t scalar[32], const uint8_t point[32])</argsstring>
        <name>syn_x25519</name>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t</type>
          <declname>shared_out</declname>
          <array>[32]</array>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const uint8_t</type>
          <declname>scalar</declname>
          <array>[32]</array>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const uint8_t</type>
          <declname>point</declname>
          <array>[32]</array>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>X25519 scalar multiplication. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Computes shared = scalar * point on Curve25519. Callers invoking <ref refid="syn__x25519_8h_1a5ebffc18301fb84fc245bc7c9a2b0f56" kindref="member">syn_x25519()</ref> directly in Diffie-Hellman protocols MUST verify in constant time that shared_out is not all-zero (RFC 7748 Section 6.1) to reject low-order input points.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>shared_out</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Output: 32-byte shared secret. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>scalar</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>32-byte private scalar (clamped internally per RFC 7748). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>point</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>32-byte public point (peer&apos;s public key). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
